# X. Episode-11 sonic conclusion

Episode 11 is one of the strongest first-cour examples of music functioning as **developmental evidence rather than narrative reward**.

The song does not merely appear after the relationship is solved.

The episode makes us hear:

- incompatible drafts;
- supportive context;
- continued disagreement;
- an initially awkward act of accommodation;
- a growing shared audience rhythm;
- a song capable of carrying both identity vocabularies;
- a fade into quiet;
- and only then explicit ratification.

The strongest retrospective formulation is therefore:

> **Asterisk becomes a unit twice: first in sound, then in administration.**

The first transformation matters more.

By the time the provisional mark acquires a name, Miku and Riina have already demonstrated that difference can be written, voiced, negotiated and performed without being erased.
